        "caption_text": "If you\u2019re tired of making the same dinners every week, save this EASY weeknight dinner. This broiled chicken thigh recipe took only 8\u201310 minutes under my broiler. 10-Minute Broiled Chicken \u2022 3.5 lbs boneless chicken thighs, cut into strips or bite-sized pieces \u2022 4 Tbsp Cajun seasoning \u2022 1-2 tsp coriander \u2022 1-2 tsp cumin \u2022 salt + pepper to taste \u2022 light coating of avocado oil + lime or lemon juice Mix everything together and marinate in the fridge for about 30 minutes. Move your oven rack to the SECOND rail from the top and spread the chicken in a single layer across your baking sheet. Turn the broiler to HIGH and broil for 8\u201310 minutes, or until the chicken reaches at least 165\u00b0. I took mine to around 175\u00b0F because thighs stay ridiculously tender and juicy and taste better above 165\u00b0 And DO NOT throw away all that seasoned juice left in the pan. \ud83e\udd24 Pour it over rice or save it for stock. You could easily change the flavor too - Adobo, Saz\u00f3n, your favorite seasoning blend\u2026 whatever your family likes. I made this batch on the nonstick baking sheet I tagged below. It\u2019s part of a 3-piece set with three different sizes, made from heavy-gauge carbon steel with a diamond-textured surface.  I also tagged the light-blocking oil sprayer I used for my avocado oil because you\u2019ll probably ask me about that too. \ud83d\ude02 Save this one for a night when you need dinner FAST. #whatsfordinner #dinnerrecipes #easydinnerideas ",
